          "explanation": "The ternary expression `(7 * 42) - num > 200` evaluates constant integers `(294 - 106 = 188 > 200)`, which is always false, but wait: 188 > 200 is false, so it chooses the false branch (`param`), NOT the constant string. Wait! Let's calculate: 7 * 42 = 294. 294 - 106 = 188. 188 > 200 is false. Therefore `bar = param`. Wait, if `bar = param`, user input reaches `fileName = Utils.TESTFILES_DIR + bar` and `new java.io.FileInputStream(fileName)`. That means it is a true positive!",
          "outcome": "genuine_dismissed",
          "reasons": [],
          "verdict": "false_positive"
        },
